    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6841" root="حب" body-key="H">
    
      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحَابَّةٌ</span></b> , (S,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحَابَبَةٌ</span>, (K,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِبَابٌ</span> signify the same [as inf. ns. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حابّ</span>]. (S, K.) [You
say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حابّ بَعْضُهُمْ بَعْضًا</span> <i>They loved, affected, liked,
approved,</i> or <i>took pleasure in, one another.</i>] And
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حابّهُ</span> <i>He acted,</i> or <i>behaved, in a loving,</i> or <i>friendly,
manner with him,</i> or <i>to him.</i> (A, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See
also 4.

